## Elastic brings prompts and token counts into trace views

Source: Elastic Observability Labs — https://www.elastic.co/observability-labs/blog/elastic-observability-9-6-apm-llm-tracing-ai-sre
Published: 2026-11-23
Channel: news

Elastic Observability is a platform for inspecting application performance and traces. Its new technical preview brings language model details into the same trace view used to investigate application requests. Elastic describes the practical problem as finding which model call in a multi-step agent consumed tokens and which prompt produced that call.

A trace waterfall displays the operations in a request over time. In the preview, its rows show input and output token counts for each model span, a record of one operation. An engineer can select a span and open its GenAI tab in Elastic APM or Discover to inspect the system prompt, user messages and model response, alongside model, provider and token usage. Copy buttons are available for the conversation fields. This lets readers compare token usage in the waterfall before opening an individual call.

The view reads OpenTelemetry's generative AI attributes, so Elastic says compatible instrumentation can come from any provider following those conventions without a proprietary SDK. Conversation content specifically requires the newer OpenTelemetry span-attribute model identified in the announcement. Elastic labels the tracing capability a technical preview and says the complete set of newly announced features is available on Elastic Cloud.

Why it matters: Teams investigating model usage in Elastic can check that their instrumentation emits the required attributes before relying on the preview's conversation and token views.

