## Phoenix reports evaluation coverage alongside acceptance results

Source: GitHub — https://github.com/Arize-ai/phoenix/releases/tag/%40arizeai/phoenix-client%408.0.3
Published: 2026-11-23
Channel: github

Arize Phoenix is an open-source platform for tracing and evaluating AI applications. Its JavaScript client now shows how broadly an acceptance criterion was recorded across an evaluation suite. A result based on only the runs with an annotation can otherwise be hard to interpret without knowing how many runs were eligible.

The release adds the number of non-skipped runs in the suite next to the number of runs that logged the criterion's annotation. The reporter presents both counts together as coverage. The release notes say the pass-or-fail calculation itself is unchanged: the criterion is still computed over the runs that recorded its annotation.

Why it matters: Engineers reviewing evaluation results can compare annotated and eligible runs before interpreting a criterion's outcome.

